\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 The framing correction\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 You do not need to build this. It is built \'97 47 files, ~2,700 lines, 60 passing tests, every module compiles. What it has never done is run against a live Postgres or a live Anthropic API.\
So the remaining work is 
\f0\b integration debugging, not construction.
\f1\b0  That distinction decides how you use Claude Code. Open a session in the repo and say "build me a nutrition tracker" and you will get a second, different codebase, because that is what the instruction asks for. Say "run this, fix what breaks" and you get the thing you already have, working.\
The repo now ships a 
\f2\fs26 CLAUDE.md
\f1\fs24  that encodes this. Claude Code reads it automatically at session start. It lists nine invariants that must not be broken, the staged order of work, and a short list of things that look like bugs but are deliberate. Do not delete it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

